<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Capabilities · Agentic Bible</title><meta name="description" content="Capabilities — Agentic Bible, a sourced reference for AI agents and their technology."><meta property="og:title" content="Capabilities · Agentic Bible"><meta property="og:description" content="Capabilities — Agentic Bible, a sourced reference for AI agents and their technology."><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Agentic Bible"><meta property="og:url" content="https://agenticbible.si/topics/capabilities/"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary"><meta name="twitter:title" content="Capabilities · Agentic Bible"><meta name="twitter:description" content="Capabilities — Agentic Bible, a sourced reference for AI agents and their technology."><meta name="robots" content="index, follow"><meta name="color-scheme" content="light"><link rel="canonical" href="https://agenticbible.si/topics/capabilities/"><link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_astro/Base.DyzAbnuc.css"></head><body><a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header shell"><a class="wordmark" href="/"><img src="/favicon.svg" width="36" height="36" alt=""><span>Agentic Bible<span class="wordmark-sub">A living reference</span></span></a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/">Library</a><a href="/topics/" aria-current="page">Topics</a><a href="/about/">About</a><a href="/history/">History</a></nav><a class="header-search" href="/search/" aria-label="Search the library"><svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"></circle><path d="m13 13 4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"></path></svg><span>Search</span><kbd aria-hidden="true">/</kbd></a></header><div class="preview-strip" role="region" aria-label="Edition status"><div class="shell"><span class="status-dot"></span> Preview edition <span class="strip-detail">Sourced working drafts. Editorial review pending.</span></div></div><main id="main" class="shell" tabindex="-1"><header class="page-intro"><a class="breadcrumb" href="/topics/">Topics / 02</a><h1>Capabilities</h1><p>How models reach beyond the conversation.</p></header><section class="topic-entries"><div class="section-heading"><h2>In this topic</h2><span>8 article</span></div><ol class="article-list"><li><span class="entry-number">02</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h3><a href="/articles/tool-use/">Tool use<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>The structured handoff between a model’s request and software that can retrieve information or take an action.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">05</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h3><a href="/articles/agent-memory/">Agent memory<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How an agent stores and retrieves information across steps or sessions, and why persistence, relevance, and truth are separate questions.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">06</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h3><a href="/articles/retrieval-augmented-generation/">Retrieval-augmented generation<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>A way to generate responses with retrieved material, with distinct failure points in finding evidence, selecting context, and using it faithfully.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">09</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h3><a href="/articles/agent-planning/">Agent planning<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How an agent represents possible steps toward a goal, checks intermediate results, and revises a course of action when assumptions fail.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">10</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h3><a href="/articles/durable-agent-execution/">Durable agent execution<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How an agent workflow records progress and resumes after interruption, while distinguishing replayed results from repeated external actions.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">12</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h3><a href="/articles/agent-sandboxing/">Agent sandboxing<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How an execution environment restricts code and tools, and why filesystem, network, resource and application boundaries need separate examination.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">16</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h3><a href="/articles/structured-outputs/">Structured outputs<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How schemas constrain the form of model responses while leaving factual correctness, supported features and execution authority as separate checks.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li><li><span class="entry-number">20</span><div class="entry-copy"><span class="eyebrow">Capabilities</span><h3><a href="/articles/computer-use-agents/">Computer-use agents<span class="entry-arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></span></a></h3><p>How agents observe and act through browser or desktop interfaces, with separate checks for screen grounding, action effects, isolation and authority.</p><span class="entry-meta">3 primary sources <span>·</span> Working draft</span></div></li></ol></section><a class="text-link back-link" href="/topics/"><svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 8H2m5-5L2 8l5 5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg> All topics</a></main><footer class="site-footer shell"><div><a class="footer-name" href="/">Agentic Bible</a><p>A little more context. A clearer understanding.</p></div><div class="footer-links"><a href="/about/#editorial">Editorial approach</a><a href="https://github.com/Leshey-Digital/agentic-bible">GitHub <svg class="icon-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 13 13 3M3 3h10v10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg></a><span>Preview · October 2026</span></div></footer><script type="module" src="/_astro/Base.astro_astro_type_script_index_0_lang.D-1rZP_q.js"></script></body></html>